{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-07 09:31:00 UTC] [Agent: Orchestrator] [Project: read_file_enhancement] User proposing dependency graph feature for read_file. Key constraint: governance-first, not visualization porn. Question: 'What decision will dependency graphs allow Scribe to ENFORCE?' Scope must stay narrow: imports only, static analysis, admit incompleteness, warnings not automation. Brainstorming integration with AST parsing. | phase=design_brainstorm; priority=low; reasoning={\"how\": \"Leverage existing AST parsing, add import extraction, build reverse lookup, integrate with scan_only discipline\", \"what\": \"Considering Tier 1 deps only: file\\u2192file, module\\u2192module, import-time relationships provable via AST\", \"why\": \"Dependency graphs can enable constraint enforcement but most implementations lie via dynamic inference\"}; scope=imports_only_static_provable; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_enhancement/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T09:31:00.622080+00:00_f047a50a", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:31:00.622106+00:00"}
