{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-07 09:42:12 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent] [Project: read_file_enhancement] Researched Python AST import nodes: ast.Import (for 'import x') and ast.ImportFrom (for 'from x import y'). Key attributes: names (list of alias nodes), module (string for ImportFrom), level (int for relative imports, 0=absolute). ImportFrom.level counts dots (from ..foo = level 2). ImportFrom.module is None for 'from . import foo'. | confidence=0.95; discovery=ast_import_nodes; reasoning={\"how\": \"Researched Python official documentation for AST import node specifications\", \"what\": \"Import and ImportFrom nodes have different attributes (level, module) that need different handling\", \"why\": \"Need to understand AST node structure before designing extraction algorithm\"}; sources=[\"https://docs.python.org/3/library/ast.html\"]; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_enhancement/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T09:42:12.895993+00:00_a96935a6", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:42:12.896021+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-07T09:42:12.895993+00:00_a96935a6", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:42:12.905654+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-07 09:42:50 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent] [Project: read_file_enhancement] Researched Python import resolution: Uses sys.modules cache \u2192 built-in modules \u2192 sys.path search. Relative imports resolve via __package__ attribute, NOT filesystem traversal. Key constraint: Static analysis can't fully resolve all imports (dynamic imports, __main__ context, sys.path modifications). Must admit incompleteness honestly. | confidence=0.9; discovery=import_resolution_limits; reasoning={\"how\": \"Researched Python official docs and PEPs to understand import system internals\", \"what\": \"Python import resolution depends on runtime state (__package__, sys.path) that static analysis can't reliably predict\", \"why\": \"Need to understand resolution algorithm to design realistic path resolver\"}; sources=[\"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/import.html\", \"https://peps.python.org/pep-0328/\"]; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_enhancement/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T09:42:50.861366+00:00_37fdc34e", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:42:50.861393+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-07T09:42:50.861366+00:00_37fdc34e", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:42:50.870845+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-07 09:42:59 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent] [Project: read_file_enhancement] Key insight: Path resolution must be BEST-EFFORT, not guaranteed. Design principle: Resolve what we can prove via static analysis (relative imports using file location, absolute imports checking repo structure), mark rest as unresolved. Honesty > completeness. Example: 'from scribe_mcp.tools.append_entry import X' can resolve if tools/append_entry.py exists in repo. | confidence=0.95; design_principle=best_effort_resolution; reasoning={\"how\": \"Derived principle from understanding Python's runtime-dependent import resolution\", \"what\": \"Resolve provable cases (relative imports, repo-local modules), admit failure for rest\", \"why\": \"Static analysis has inherent limits - must design for realistic boundaries\"}; stage=research; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_enhancement/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T09:42:59.698736+00:00_4daed089", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:42:59.698761+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-07T09:42:59.698736+00:00_4daed089", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:42:59.707989+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-07 09:43:25 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent] [Project: read_file_enhancement] Designing response schema for dependency analysis. Structure: dependencies dict with imports[], relative_imports[], total_imports count, unresolved[] list, truncated flag. Each import entry contains: module, line, type (import;from_import;import_as), names[], resolved_path (if resolvable), alias (if applicable), level (for relative). | confidence=0.9; design_artifact=response_schema; reasoning={\"how\": \"Designed schema based on AST node attributes and path resolution capabilities\", \"what\": \"Schema separates absolute/relative imports, tracks resolution success/failure, preserves line numbers for navigation\", \"why\": \"Need structured response format for downstream consumption by agents and tooling\"}; stage=research; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_enhancement/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T09:43:25.686024+00:00_f14cdd91", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:43:25.686049+00:00"}
