{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-07 09:43:39 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent] [Project: read_file_enhancement] Researching governance use cases for dependency analysis. Primary use cases: (1) Impact radius warnings - 'This file imported by X modules, touch carefully', (2) Boundary enforcement - detect forbidden cross-boundary imports (sentinel\u2192tools violation), (3) Dead code detection - files with zero imports are deletion candidates, (4) Checklist triggers - editing high-impact files requires review checklist. | confidence=0.95; discovery=governance_use_cases; reasoning={\"how\": \"Analyzed user requirements and cross-referenced with existing Scribe governance patterns\", \"what\": \"Four key governance patterns: impact warnings, boundary detection, dead code flagging, checklist triggering\", \"why\": \"Dependency graphs must enable ENFORCEMENT decisions, not just visualization\"}; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_enhancement/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T09:43:39.663579+00:00_294a8700", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:43:39.663607+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-07T09:43:39.663579+00:00_294a8700", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:43:39.673143+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-07 09:43:56 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent] [Project: read_file_enhancement] Documenting implementation phases. Phase 1: Add include_dependencies parameter, implement _extract_imports() for basic AST import extraction, return in response payload, update readable formatter. Phase 2: Add _resolve_import_path() for best-effort path resolution, handle relative imports, mark unresolved honestly. Phase 3 (future): Build reverse lookup index, show 'imported by X files' warnings. Phase 4 (future): Boundary enforcement via config. Phase 5 (future): Dead code detection. STOP AFTER PHASE 2 per user directive. | confidence=0.95; design_artifact=implementation_phases; reasoning={\"how\": \"Structured phases by increasing complexity and risk, with natural stopping point after basic functionality\", \"what\": \"5 phases defined, phases 1-2 for initial implementation, phases 3-5 for future enhancement based on usage\", \"why\": \"Need clear phase boundaries to prevent scope creep and enable iterative refinement\"}; stage=research; stopping_point=phase_2; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_enhancement/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T09:43:56.917291+00:00_a51466a9", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:43:56.917323+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-07T09:43:56.917291+00:00_a51466a9", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:43:56.926940+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-07 09:44:11 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent] [Project: read_file_enhancement] Defining critical boundaries - what NOT to do. Forbidden: (1) Function-level call graphs (dynamic dispatch lies), (2) Higher-order functions/runtime behavior, (3) Conditional imports (if __name__), (4) Dynamic imports (importlib), (5) Reflection/monkey patching, (6) 'Complete' dependency claims. Rationale: Python's dynamic nature makes these unprovable via static analysis. Attempting = false confidence. | confidence=1; design_artifact=forbidden_patterns; reasoning={\"how\": \"Identified patterns that violate 'static analysis only' and 'admit incompleteness' constraints\", \"what\": \"Six categories of forbidden analysis that would require runtime introspection or lie about completeness\", \"why\": \"Must establish clear boundaries to prevent feature creep into unreliable territory\"}; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_enhancement/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T09:44:11.536610+00:00_658fc183", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:44:11.536711+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-07T09:44:11.536610+00:00_658fc183", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:44:11.546500+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-07 09:44:31 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent] [Project: read_file_enhancement] Designing readable mode output for dependencies. When include_dependencies=False (default): no change, fast scan. When True: Add '\ud83d\udce6 Dependencies:' section after file structure, display imports with line numbers, show resolved paths with \u2192 arrow, mark external stdlib/packages as [external], list unresolved imports, show truncation if needed. Format: '\u2022 module_name (line 42) \u2192 path/to/file.py' or '\u2022 module_name (line 42) [external stdlib]'. | confidence=0.9; design_artifact=readable_output_format; reasoning={\"how\": \"Based on existing readable formatter patterns for structure analysis (functions/classes/headings)\", \"what\": \"Designed section layout, line number integration, path display conventions, external/unresolved marking\", \"why\": \"Readable mode must display dependencies in agent-friendly format consistent with existing structure display\"}; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_enhancement/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T09:44:31.382554+00:00_a8a4e1ee", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:44:31.382582+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-07T09:44:31.382554+00:00_a8a4e1ee", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:44:31.392103+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-07 09:44:47 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent] [Project: read_file_enhancement] Analyzing performance implications. include_dependencies=False (default): Zero overhead, same fast scan as current. include_dependencies=True: Additional cost for import extraction (~5-10% overhead for AST node iteration), path resolution filesystem checks (can be expensive for large repos). Mitigation: (1) Opt-in flag keeps default fast, (2) Leverage existing parsed AST tree (no double parsing), (3) Cache path resolution within single scan, (4) Limit import count with truncation (like functions/classes). | confidence=0.85; discovery=performance_analysis; reasoning={\"how\": \"Analyzed AST parsing cost, filesystem check overhead, designed caching and truncation strategies\", \"what\": \"Identified overhead sources and mitigation strategies to maintain acceptable performance\", \"why\": \"Performance is critical constraint - must not degrade default experience\"}; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_enhancement/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T09:44:47.084884+00:00_ba5f553b", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:44:47.084913+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-07T09:44:47.084884+00:00_ba5f553b", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:44:47.096035+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-07 09:44:55 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent] [Project: read_file_enhancement] Designing testing strategy. Phase 1 tests: (1) Basic import extraction - verify ast.Import and ast.ImportFrom nodes detected, (2) Line number accuracy, (3) Alias handling (import x as y), (4) Relative import level detection (., .., ...). Phase 2 tests: (5) Path resolution for repo-local modules, (6) Relative import resolution, (7) External/stdlib detection, (8) Unresolved import tracking, (9) Performance regression testing (ensure <20% overhead). Test files: Use existing scribe_mcp Python files as real-world test cases. | confidence=0.9; design_artifact=testing_strategy; reasoning={\"how\": \"Designed tests based on AST node types, resolution scenarios, and performance constraints\", \"what\": \"9 test categories covering extraction accuracy, resolution correctness, performance boundaries\", \"why\": \"Need comprehensive test coverage to validate correctness and performance\"}; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_enhancement/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T09:44:55.795264+00:00_abf90b60", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T09:44:55.795291+00:00"}
