{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-07 10:35:46 UTC] [Agent: CoderAgent-Phase1] [Project: read_file_enhancement] \u2705 Task 1B complete: Implemented _extract_imports() AST function. Extracts import and from_import statements with full metadata (module, line, type, names, alias, level). Handles both ast.Import and ast.ImportFrom nodes. Respects max_imports limit (100 default). Returns list of dicts matching architecture schema. | files_changed=[\"tools/read_file.py\"]; function=_extract_imports; lines_added=62; reasoning={\"how\": \"Used ast.walk() to traverse tree, handled both Import and ImportFrom nodes separately, matched exact schema from architecture guide lines 101-109, added comprehensive docstring\", \"what\": \"Created _extract_imports function accepting AST tree; walks tree to find ast.Import and ast.ImportFrom nodes; extracts module, line, type, names, alias, level; respects max_imports truncation\", \"why\": \"Enable AST-based extraction of Python import statements for dependency discovery\"}; task=1B; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_enhancement/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T10:35:46.716699+00:00_b0c7ed3a", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T10:35:46.716728+00:00"}
