{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-07 11:29:56 UTC] [Agent: Orchestrator] [Project: read_file_enhancement] Carl's review received: Phase 2 approved as \"structurally useful solid\" - crossed from file viewer to static analysis tool. Key wins: scan mode doing real work (cheap/fast/structural), dependency grouping clean, function index enables jump navigation, metadata enables integrity/caching. Risks flagged: third-party overloaded (needs internal vs external split later), imports \u2260 dependencies (syntactic only), output powerful enough to mislead dumb agents. Strategic read: building file profiler/scout correctly without premature complexity. Question posed: AST usage mapping vs cross-file graphing - which first? | grade_informal=solid; key_wins=5; phase=phase_2_carl_review; review_source=Carl; risks_flagged=3; strategic_question=ast_usage_vs_cross_file_graphing; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_enhancement/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T11:29:56.294710+00:00_5ab63bb5", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T11:29:56.294740+00:00"}
