{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-07 12:17:20 UTC] [Agent: CoderAgent-Phase4] [Project: read_file_enhancement] Task 4C COMPLETE! Added _check_boundary_violations() function (120 lines) to tools/read_file.py. Algorithm: (1) Iterate rules, check if file matches source pattern, (2) For matched files, check each import against forbidden_imports patterns (both path-based and module-based), (3) Respect allowed_exceptions, (4) Return violations with rule_name/severity/violated_import/message/line. Handles both glob patterns (tools/**) and module patterns (scribe_mcp.tools.*). Ready for Task 4D: response schema integration. | lines_added=120; phase=4_part2_boundary; reasoning={\"how\": \"Iterate rules, pattern-match source files, check imports (path or module patterns), handle exceptions, return violation list\", \"what\": \"Violation checker that matches files to rules, then checks imports against forbidden patterns with exception support\", \"why\": \"Need to identify forbidden import patterns automatically during scans\"}; task=4C_complete; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/read_file_enhancement/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T12:17:20.428501+00:00_3dda5870", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T12:17:20.428530+00:00"}
